course: dictionary
lesson: 4155
title: A glyph is a sign
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A glyph is a picture or symbol that stands for a word, a sound or an idea. When you meet an unknown word, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs, carved on stone and painted in folding books made of bark.» The clues are carved, painted and writing system, so a glyph must be a mark people made to write with.
explain: The word also works in computers. A glyph is the shape drawn for a letter, number or symbol in a particular font. The letter A looks different in each font, and each look is a glyph.
fact: Glyph means a picture or symbol used as a sign for a word, a sound or an idea.
fact: Egyptian hieroglyphs and Maya glyphs are carved or painted signs from ancient times.
fact: In computing, a glyph is the drawn shape of a letter, number or symbol in a font.
fact: Emojis are glyphs too, because each one is a picture used as a sign.
fact: «Deciphered» means worked out, so «mostly been deciphered» means people have mostly figured out what the Maya glyphs say.
exercise: «The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs, carved on stone.» What is a glyph? | *A picture or symbol used as a sign for a word, a sound or an idea | A kind of stone used for building | A loud musical instrument | A kind of bark used to make books
exercise: In a computer, what is a glyph? | *The shape drawn for a letter, number or symbol in a particular font | The name of a computer game | A tiny memory chip
exercise: Which word in «The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs» tells you glyphs were part of a way of writing? | glyphs | Maya | stone | *writing
test: In computing, what is each different look of the letter A called? | A byte | A font | A pixel | *A glyph
test: Which of these is a glyph? | *A smiley emoji | A tall tree | A page number in a book | A wooden table
exam: Which answer best describes a glyph in «The Maya had a full writing system of glyphs»? | *A sign that stands for a word, a sound or an idea | A kind of stone floor | A type of food | A game played with cards
